@ Wavy liquids (code/tweaks/wavy_liquids.cpp). Every entry is a `push`, so the trampolines can
@ replay it.

@ Water::onCreate (Water vtable 0x60C08888 slot 5). Entry: push {r4-r10, lr}.
WavyLiquids_water:
    type:       hook
    address:    0x005AB2AC
    symbol:     ModBase::waves::waterCreate(StageActor*)
    trampoline: ModBase::waves::waterCreate_orig(StageActor*)

@ Poison::onCreate. Entry: push {r4-r6, lr}.
WavyLiquids_poison:
    type:       hook
    address:    0x005A9A20
    symbol:     ModBase::waves::poisonCreate(StageActor*)
    trampoline: ModBase::waves::poisonCreate_orig(StageActor*)

@ Quicksand::onCreate. Entry: push {r4-r10, lr}.
WavyLiquids_quicksand:
    type:       hook
    address:    0x005AA7A4
    symbol:     ModBase::waves::quicksandCreate(StageActor*)
    trampoline: ModBase::waves::quicksandCreate_orig(StageActor*)

@ TerrainEffects::update. Entry: push {r4-r9, r11, lr}.
WavyLiquids_update:
    type:       hook
    address:    0x00705F6C
    symbol:     ModBase::waves::update(void*)
    trampoline: ModBase::waves::update_orig(void*)


@ Wave collision liquid (Tsuru's WaveCollision patches): where checkWaveCollision (0x60151D34) finds
@ a point inside the waves, CollisionMgr answers lava (3, or 4 by TileMgr +0x2820) whatever the
@ liquid. Both sites (0x60151F18 and 0x60152338: movw r0, #0x2820; ldrb r0, [r1, r0]; cmp r0, #0;
@ moveq r0, #3; movne r0, #4; then the result is stored and the function returns) now call
@ ModBase::waves::waveLiquid(r0, r1 = TileMgr), which answers the zone's own liquid type
@ (TileMgr +0x2824) for a non-lava liquid.

WaveCollision1_call:
    type:    call
    address: 0x00151F18
    symbol:  ModBase::waves::waveLiquid(int, unsigned char*)

WaveCollision1_nop1:
    type:         instr
    instruction:  nop
    address:      0x00151F1C

WaveCollision1_nop2:
    type:         instr
    instruction:  nop
    address:      0x00151F20

WaveCollision1_nop3:
    type:         instr
    instruction:  nop
    address:      0x00151F24

WaveCollision1_nop4:
    type:         instr
    instruction:  nop
    address:      0x00151F28

WaveCollision2_call:
    type:    call
    address: 0x00152338
    symbol:  ModBase::waves::waveLiquid(int, unsigned char*)

WaveCollision2_nop1:
    type:         instr
    instruction:  nop
    address:      0x0015233C

WaveCollision2_nop2:
    type:         instr
    instruction:  nop
    address:      0x00152340

WaveCollision2_nop3:
    type:         instr
    instruction:  nop
    address:      0x00152344

WaveCollision2_nop4:
    type:         instr
    instruction:  nop
    address:      0x00152348

@ TerrainEffects::draw: a wavy liquid's body is drawn too. Entry: push {r4-r8, lr}.
WavyLiquids_draw:
    type:       hook
    address:    0x00707390
    symbol:     ModBase::waves::draw(void*)
    trampoline: ModBase::waves::draw_orig(void*)
